{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.RossmannCCBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.RossmannCCBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Group.Int","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.rossmann_cc_two_parity_fails","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.rossmann_cc_two_parity_fails","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/RossmannCCBridge.lean#L107-L117","doc":"The concentration is **not vacuous as an implication**: the same hypotheses\nwithout single-parity do NOT force `e - o = Δ_λ`.  A two-parity witness\n(`e = o = 1`, `dim = 2`, `target = 2`) satisfies every field EXCEPT\n`single_parity`, yet `e - o = 0 ≠ 2 = target` — mirroring #4581's cancellation.\nSo `single_parity` (IDENT) is genuinely load-bearing in the derivation above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.rossmann_cc_realizes_deltaLambda","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.rossmann_cc_realizes_deltaLambda","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/RossmannCCBridge.lean#L79-L105","doc":"**Conditional consequence (DERIVED, non-degenerate).**  Given (IDENT) — the\narchimedean character's characteristic cycle is single grade-parity — its signed\nEuler characteristic `e - o` equals `Δ_λ`.  I.e. the characteristic cycle\n**realizes** `Δ_λ`: the single-degree concentration (`DeltaLambdaDTRealization`)\nholds *conditionally on (IDENT)*.\n\nThe derivation is genuine (not a projection of the hypothesis): single-parity\ngives the saturation `|e - o| = e + o = dim = |Δ_λ|`, and `sign_match` upgrades\nequal-magnitude to equal-signed. The open input is `single_parity` (IDENT); the\nconclusion `e - o = Δ_λ` is composed from it with the proved corpus prerequisites\n`total`/`target_abs` (the #4581 single-parity-saturation mechanism, over `ℤ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.RossmannCCConcentration.sign_match","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.RossmannCCConcentration.sign_match","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/RossmannCCBridge.lean#L75-L75","doc":"The cycle's signed Euler characteristic has the sign of `Δ_λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.RossmannCCConcentration.single_parity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.RossmannCCConcentration.single_parity","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/RossmannCCBridge.lean#L73-L73","doc":"**(IDENT) — the open substrate identification.**  The characteristic cycle\nof the archimedean character is single grade-parity (cancellation-free). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.RossmannCCConcentration.target_abs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.RossmannCCConcentration.target_abs","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/RossmannCCBridge.lean#L70-L70","doc":"`Δ_λ` is the signed dimension. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.RossmannCCConcentration.total","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.RossmannCCConcentration.total","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/RossmannCCBridge.lean#L68-L68","doc":"Proved-in-corpus prerequisite: `f_λ(1) = dim V_λ` (ungraded total). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.RossmannCCConcentration.o_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.RossmannCCConcentration.o_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/RossmannCCBridge.lean#L66-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.RossmannCCConcentration.e_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.RossmannCCConcentration.e_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/RossmannCCBridge.lean#L65-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.RossmannCCConcentration.o","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.RossmannCCConcentration.o","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/RossmannCCBridge.lean#L64-L64","doc":"Odd-cohomological-degree mass of the characteristic cycle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.RossmannCCConcentration.e","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.RossmannCCConcentration.e","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/RossmannCCBridge.lean#L62-L62","doc":"Even-cohomological-degree mass of the characteristic cycle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.RossmannCCConcentration.target","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.RossmannCCConcentration.target","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/RossmannCCBridge.lean#L60-L60","doc":"The signed binding factor `Δ_λ` (`= ±dim`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.RossmannCCConcentration.dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.RossmannCCConcentration.dim","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/RossmannCCBridge.lean#L58-L58","doc":"Wedderburn dimension `dim V_λ` (as a `ℤ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.RossmannCCConcentration.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.RossmannCCConcentration.mk","kind":"ctor","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/RossmannCCBridge.lean#L56-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.RossmannCCConcentration","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.RossmannCCConcentration","kind":"class","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/RossmannCCBridge.lean#L42-L75","doc":"**Conditional conjecture class (§3b-cond, OPEN — no instance).**\n\nFor each partition datum `l : Λ`, the archimedean character's Springer\ncharacteristic cycle is summarised by its **even-degree mass** `e l ≥ 0` and\n**odd-degree mass** `o l ≥ 0` (of cohomological degree); its ungraded total\n`e + o` is the Wedderburn dimension `dim l` (a proved-in-corpus prerequisite);\nits signed Euler characteristic is `e - o`; and `target l = Δ_λ` is the signed\ndimension (`|target| = dim`), sign-matched to the cycle.\n\nThe **content field is `single_parity` — this is (IDENT)**: the claim that the\ncharacteristic cycle of the archimedean character is *single grade-parity*\n(concentrated / cancellation-free), the microlocal concentration Rossmann +\nSpringer predict for a genuine invariant eigendistribution.  It is the OPEN\nsubstrate identification; there is deliberately **no instance** of this class. ","signatureChunk":0}]}